;;; A hypothesis `(absent (paid ?g))` split R on a fact nothing reads —
;;; regression `absent-hrule-concluded`.
;;;
;;; ── What this program is ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; Two guests and a hypothesis rule that supposes `(absent (paid ?g))` of each.
;;;
;;; ── The answer, by hand ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; No fact is headed `absent`, so no hypothesis is: `(open (absent …))` is refused
;;; at the parse, on every command (Q-M1f.568).
;;;
;;; ── What the engine answered ──────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; At `52e05fc1`, release: the program loaded; H was `(absent (paid Ann))` and
;;; `(absent (paid Bob))`, and R four states that differ only in facts of `absent`,
;;; which no premise can read: the goal had no row in any, exit 0 on every command.
;;; The engine now refuses it at the parse, on every command.
;;;

(relation paid Guest :why "{?3} has paid")
(is-a Ann Guest) (is-a Bob Guest)
(rule guess () :match (is-a ?g Guest) :assert (open (absent (paid ?g))) :why "suppose {?g} has not paid")
(query :goal (paid ?g))
